<a id="policy-int_routed_host"></a>
### Policy: int_routed_host

The following parameters are supported when using the `int_routed_host` policy:

- `vrf` - Interface VRF (Interface VRF name, default VRF if not specified)
- `ipv4_address` - Interface IP (IP address of the interface)
- `ipv4_prefix_length` - IP Netmask Length (IP netmask length used with the IP address (Min:1, Max:31))
- `routing_tag` - Routing TAG (Routing tag associated with interface IP)
- `mtu` - MTU (MTU for the interface (Min:576, Max:9216)) (Default: 9216)
- `disable_ip_redirects` - Disable IP Redirects (Disable both IPv4/IPv6 redirects on the interface) (Default: false)
- `enable_pim_sparse` - Enable PIM Sparse-mode (Enable PIM sparse-mode on the interface) (Default: false)
- `pim_dr_priority` - PIM DR Priority (<1-4294967295> Configure priority for PIM DR election on the interface, default is 1) (Default: 1)
- `netflow` - Enable Netflow (Netflow is supported only if it is enabled on fabric) (Default: false)
- `netflow_monitor` - Netflow Monitor (Provide the Layer 3 Monitor Name)
- `netflow_sampler` - Netflow Sampler (Netflow sampler name, applicable to N7K only)
- `enable_pfc` - Enable priority flow control (Enable priority flow control) (Default: false)
- `enable_qos` - Enable QoS Configuration (Enable to configure a QoS Policy for this interface. If AI/ML Queuing is enabled on the fabric, will use the QOS_CLASSIFICATION policy. Enter a custom policy below to override) (Default: false)
- `qos_policy` - Custom QoS Policy (Custom QoS Policy must be defined previously)
- `queuing_policy` - Custom Queuing Policy  (Queuing Policy must be defined previously)

<a id="policy-int_shared_trunk_host"></a>
### Policy: int_shared_trunk_host

The following parameters are supported when using the `int_shared_trunk_host` policy:

